            <ArticleTitle>Same-Day Discharge After Transradial Percutaneous Coronary Intervention and Carotid Stenting in a Single Session.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>830.e1-830.e3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0828-282X(17)30033-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cjca.2016.12.021</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Same-day discharge after combined percutaneous carotid and coronary stenting in a single session has not been previously reported. Using a transradial approach, we completed both procedures successfully and the 63-year-old patient was discharged home after a few hours. This case illustrates that radial access allows treatment of complex coronary and peripheral lesions in a same setting and could provide clinical and cost benefits if safety is confirmed.</AbstractText>
